            <div xml:id="d124">

                <pb facs="0177" n="165" xml:id="pg165"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Athens Embassy Files, 1945, 800 Elections</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Greece</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >MacVeagh</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to Archbishop Damaskinos, Regent of
                        Greece</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Athens</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-09-27">September 27,
                        1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Your Beatitude</hi>: I have the honor to inform Your
                    Beatitude that I have now received a message from the Secretary of State of the
                    United States of America, Mr. Byrnes, instructing me to concert with my
                    colleagues of Great Britain and France in regard to impressing upon the Greek
                    political leaders the need for them to cooperate over the forthcoming elections
                    with a view to the eventual establishment of a stable government in this
                    country.</p>
                <p>I am communicating this to Your Beatitude because of Your Beatitude’s request to
                    Mr. Byrnes and the promise which he gave Your Beatitude in this connection. As I
                    informed Your Beatitude last Monday I was not then in receipt of instructions,
                    but since receiving them I have already started to confer with my colleagues,
                    and I feel it is unnecessary to assure Your Beatitude that I shall carry out the
                    Secretary’s instructions to the best of my ability.</p>
                <p>I beg Your Beatitude to accept my highest expressions of respect.</p>
                <closer>[<signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lincoln MacVeagh</hi>
                    </signed>]</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
